&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We at Peloton are looking for a scrappy, creative and fast-moving AI Engineer.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll take raw ideas and rapidly transform them into production-grade applications that empower our global organization. You will architect the Intelligence &amp;amp; Integration Layers that connect autonomous agents directly into Peloton’s enterprise infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We don&#39;t care about your specific stack or what programming language you grew up with. We care about systems thinking, engineering fundamentals, product instinct and your ability to ship fast.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR DAILY IMPACT AT PELOTON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ambiguous problems and turn them into functional, high-performing AI features and standalone tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement standardized integration layers connecting agents to core enterprise systems using secure protocols like MCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve the &quot;State Problem&quot; for AI by building memory architectures and vector stores (Pinecone, Pgvector) that maintain context while strictly adhering to data retention and deletion policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Security to implement Identity Propagation (e.g., OAuth On-Behalf-Of flows) and RBAC. Ensure agents execute tasks strictly using the user’s specific permissions, eliminating privilege escalation risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build &quot;Data Clean Rooms&quot; and automated PII masking/redaction pipelines to guarantee that sensitive member, employee, or proprietary financial data is never exposed to external model providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure all AI workflows comply with enterprise regulatory standards and internal data governance policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploy continuous evaluation pipelines to test models for hallucinations, prompt injections, data leakage, and performance regressions before code hits production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement Semantic Caching and smart routing logic (directing routine queries to smaller, cheaper models) to maintain low latency and efficient inference costs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in creating templates, SDKs, and libraries that enable non-engineers and analysts to &quot;vibe code&quot; and prototype safely without bypassing compliance or security controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU BRING TO PELOTON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7+ Years of General Software Engineering: Strong foundational software engineering skills (distributed systems, async patterns, API design, microservices, and databases)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Language-Agnostic Mindset: Deep fluency in Python or Go, but comfortable pivoting to whatever language or framework gets the job done fastest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production AI Execution: Hands-on experience deploying RAG (Retrieval-Augmented Generation) and Agentic Workflows into production using LLM APIs, vector databases, and orchestration frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;div&gt;
