&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Join the Peloton Product Engineering team within our Connected Fitness organization and help build the core software powering the screens of our flagship hardware. In this role, you will develop the primary, member-facing application embedded on every Peloton Bike, Tread, and Row. This is your opportunity to shape the on-equipment software that delivers our best-in-class fitness experiences directly to millions of Members worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR DAILY IMPACT AT PELOTON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build highly engaging, responsive, and scalable customer-facing features from concept to deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide, mentor, and elevate mid-level and junior engineers while optimizing team processes and modernizing engineering solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, UX, and Design teams to evaluate execution feasibility, manage cross-team dependencies, and translate vision into clean code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently tackle complex engineering tasks, leveraging AI-first coding tools (like Claude Code) and profiling UI, memory, and threading to ensure a flawless user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOU BRING TO PELOTON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of software development experience, including 4+ years of dedicated Android development, backed by a B.S. in Computer Science/Engineering (or equivalent experience). Experience with continuous build integration in an Agile environment, active GitHub projects, or open-source contributions is highly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of Kotlin, Java, Android threading, and modern architecture patterns like MVVM and MVI. Familiarity with automation testing frameworks like Espresso is a major plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience interacting with REST APIs, handling data processing, and evaluating complex engineering trade-offs. Exposure to modern data query languages like gRPC and GraphQL is a distinct advantage&lt;/li&gt;
