&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT THE ROLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Peloton is looking for a Sr. Category Manager, Indirect Sourcing &amp;amp; Procurement to join our Global Procurement team.&amp;nbsp; This individual manages the overall direction-process and spend associated with Peloton’s purchases for assigned categories. This role will be accountable for building strong relationships with business stakeholders and partnering with them to establish a cohesive supplier portfolio and spend category strategies based on business needs - market segmentation assessments, supplier spend and concentration analyses, total cost modeling across different functions and regions for multiple categories purchases to enable timely and efficient growth of our business including identifying business requirements and specifications, developing and implementing sourcing strategies, conducting cost evaluations, managing RFx, and leading contract negotiations for all assigned categories and drive execution of the objectives aligned with Peloton&#39;s goals. Must be results-driven about business cost reduction, revenue increasing initiatives, aggregating supplier volume/reducing price, and identifying new opportunities. Work closely with team leads, budget owners, and leadership throughout the assigned categories.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;YOUR DAILY IMPACT AT PELOTON&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively support the development of sourcing strategies using Peloton global spend where possible, translate strategy into objectives/action plans, and drive execution of the objectives for logistics and distribution categories aligned with the business/sourcing strategy and company goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Optimize total direct and indirect costs for the business while collaborating with stakeholders of assigned categories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead sourcing efforts and direct the execution of effective cost saving initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effectively lead/project manage cross-functional teams through RFP process including requirements definition, bid/negotiations, contract documentation, and integration ensuring appropriate approvals are acquired&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the scaling of Peloton’s capabilities by finding opportunities for efficiencies and operational improvements&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Responsible for commercial terms negotiations of price, terms, and the scope of services, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure sourcing and other procurement activity is aligned with SOX and appropriate internal Peloton controls for segregation of duties and appropriate fiduciary controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and direct the execution of effective cost savings initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication of cost savings initiatives through leadership participation and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct and manage logistics provider Quarterly Business Reviews for top providers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Align closely with trade compliance function to ensure providers are following international trade laws and Peloton policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and supervise process improvements, training, and talent development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
